  "title": "WorldCycle and CoCo for Action-Controllable World Models",
  "summary": "WorldCycle introduces a self-verifiable reinforcement learning framework to address the verification bottleneck in long-horizon video world models, enabling action cycles to be validated without requiring ground-truth future states. CoCo enhances action controllability by enforcing counterfactual consistency and spatial consistency constraints, improving both action predictability and performance across different action types.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "WorldCycle reduces state returning drift by up to 44% and lifts composite-action accuracy nearly 4x over the base model.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "CoCo introduces Counterfactual Consistency and Action-Spatial Consistency constraints to enhance action controllability.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "WorldCycle and CoCo are developed to address the limitations of statistical shortcuts in action-conditioned world models.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
